# Where the contact form POSTs submissions.
#
# The site is a static bundle served by nginx — it has no backend of its own,
# so sending mail requires a third-party form endpoint. Any service that accepts
# a JSON POST works; these are the common ones:
#
#   Formspree    https://formspree.io      -> https://formspree.io/f/<your-id>
#   Web3Forms    https://web3forms.com     -> https://api.web3forms.com/submit
#   Formsubmit   https://formsubmit.co     -> https://formsubmit.co/ajax/<email>
#
# The form sends { name, email, subject, message } as JSON.
#
# Leave this unset and the form falls back to opening the visitor's mail client
# with the message prefilled — it still works, it just relies on them having one.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in your endpoint. Vite
# inlines the value at BUILD time, so rebuild the Docker image after changing it.
VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=
